# UI (design system & styling)

## Component locations

- **Primitives:** `src/components/ui/` (Button, Container, Section, Eyebrow, Reveal).
- **Chrome:** `src/components/layout/` (Header, Footer, MobileCTABar, LegalShell).
- **Page sections:** `src/components/sections/`, each driven by a module in `src/content/`.
- **Frozen brand asset:** `src/components/design/Brand.tsx`. Do not move or edit it; `npm run brand:check` enforces its viewBox.
- Prefer **extending** these components over introducing parallel primitives or a second UI kit.

## Visual system

- **Tailwind CSS v4** with tokens and imports in `src/app/globals.css` and `src/styles/fonts.css`.
- Do **not** introduce another CSS framework, component library, or icon set unless the user explicitly requests it. Icons are **`lucide-react`** in line with the rest of the repo.

## Motion

- Use **`motion/react`** and shared **`Variants`** from `@/lib/motion`—keep easing, blur, and offset patterns aligned with existing variants.

## Brand and fonts

- **Brand guard** (`npm run brand:check`, `scripts/brand-guard.mjs`) enforces fonts, `globals.css` imports, and logo constants. After touching fonts, CSS variables, `Brand.tsx`, or font loading in `layout.tsx`, run the brand check.
- Root **`.cursorrules`** lists additional brand constraints (e.g. baseline font loading approach).

## Content and layout

- Marketing copy, URLs, phone, email, and nav structure should flow from **`src/lib/site.ts`** where possible—avoid hardcoding duplicate brand strings.

## Editing discipline

- **Inspect** sibling sections and reused components before changing spacing, typography, or color.
- **Incremental** styling changes; preserve accessibility patterns already present (landmarks, labels, widget behavior).
- **Do not delete** compliance- or accessibility-related markup unless explicitly instructed.

## No duplication of stack docs

- Detailed analytics, legal pages, and metadata rules live in **`.cursorrules`**—this file focuses on **UI structure, Tailwind, motion, and brand** without re-stating every SEO/legal bullet.
